      <data key="d5">1756461338</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Clause 2.3">
      <data key="d0">Clause 2.3</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Clause 2.3 encompasses a comprehensive framework for site and context analysis pertinent to development projects. It outlines zoning regulations applicable to various residential and commercial zones as stipulated in the State Environmental Planning Policy (Biodiversity and Conservation) 2021. Additionally, Clause 2.3 includes specific guidelines from the Marrickville Development Control Plan (DCP) 2011, which address critical aspects of site context analysis, such as setbacks, height limits, and environmental protection measures. Furthermore, it specifies regulations concerning side setbacks for new buildings or additions that are visible from the street, ensuring that developments align with the established planning and environmental standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Clause 2.3 outlines zoning and land use provisions under the State Environmental Planning Policy (Biodiversity and Conservation) 2021.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-489fcda892097faf351f3c6138355afb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bcafac0958c581e47c81e3b4834154f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7320711159fac7b8b992e31aa693fc92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b3e7253c92605b170ab298351d159ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e31559520dd19b21fb017451dd55e77f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
