    <node id="Child Care Centres">
      <data key="d0">Child Care Centres</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Child Care Centres refers to the regulations and guidelines for the establishment of child care facilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Child care centres are facilities that provide care and education for children, operating under specific zoning and development application requirements. In the Inner West, these centres are permitted under the Inner West LEP 2022, which includes particular stipulations regarding parking and heritage compliance. Additionally, they are regulated by the Marrickville DCP, which outlines requirements for their location and the impact they may have on residential amenity. Overall, child care centres must adhere to strict regulations concerning their construction and operation, especially in residential zones, to ensure they meet community standards and maintain a harmonious living environment.</data>
