    <node id="Heritage Items">
      <data key="d0">Heritage Items</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Heritage Items are significant buildings or structures located within designated precincts that hold historical, architectural, and cultural value. These items are recognized for their importance and are protected under the guidelines of the Marrickville Development Control Plan (DCP) and local planning regulations. The preservation of Heritage Items is essential to maintain their historical significance and cultural integrity, ensuring that these important structures and sites are safeguarded for future generations. Development activities involving Heritage Items must reflect and complement their identified historical significance and values, thereby contributing to the ongoing protection and appreciation of these vital features within the precinct. Overall, Heritage Items encompass specific structures or features recognized for their historical or cultural value within conservation areas, highlighting their role in the community's heritage and identity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fa8775a9fb88eae75c0cecab2248a9b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3cee99042961089995b14fb3bff5ef4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a31ca0ad7ef033136702ccbb86559a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-138453762007b334057c50ce82e9281b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a078e25ceef9568a7e493f605b59504b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fa8d35270c594182dd4ccb9613538b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cf7ce8c5c0949b1b86a8e47f7228f94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22bb41e5d9af8e1f44c220ea3ef55754&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87f3217d092603d5e1a949d5ef9939fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8efad060b56eb835502c34ac1ab1936d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1da8d672287b53e3db6d48ae3938e2e8</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1756462306</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Heritage Conservation Areas">
      <data key="d0">Heritage Conservation Areas</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Heritage Conservation Areas are designated regions aimed at preserving the heritage significance of buildings, sites, and archaeological locations. These areas are established to ensure that development is responsive to their heritage significance, thereby maintaining the character and identity of neighborhoods through specific regulations. Furthermore, Heritage Conservation Areas require the preservation and enhancement of their historical and architectural significance, as well as the safeguarding of historical and cultural values in any development activities. In particular, within the Leichhardt area, these designated regions necessitate the protection of their historical significance, reinforcing the commitment to heritage conservation in the community.&lt;SEP&gt;Heritage Conservation Areas are designated regions that require development to be responsive to their heritage significance.&lt;SEP&gt;Heritage Conservation Areas are designated regions that require special consideration to preserve their historical and cultural significance, particularly regarding signage and development.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e58bf8dbb5246c231cdb11e6a2798a16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a31ca0ad7ef033136702ccbb86559a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72f295e95bd32e9a02119f496cba255c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-582fa0b062972c42620f6cc6ea46eb56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed559eb921e82179a5ab2b83d8456566&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22bb41e5d9af8e1f44c220ea3ef55754&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a508bfc5d79a3f8e112147c41e0822e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-559fa0a250051042f9354b0984303a96</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1756462613</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Australia International Council on Monuments and Sites (ICOMOS)">
      <data key="d0">Australia International Council on Monuments and Sites (ICOMOS)</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">ICOMOS is an organization that provides guidelines for the conservation of places of cultural significance, including the Burra Charter.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-582fa0b062972c42620f6cc6ea46eb56</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1756460767</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Burra Charter">
      <data key="d0">Burra Charter</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The Burra Charter is a document that guides heritage conservation practices in Australia, emphasizing the importance of managing heritage values.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-582fa0b062972c42620f6cc6ea46eb56</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1756460767</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Ashfield LEP">
      <data key="d0">Ashfield LEP</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Ashfield LEP is a local environmental plan that includes provisions for heritage items and conservation areas within its jurisdiction.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-582fa0b062972c42620f6cc6ea46eb56</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1756460767</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Inner West Ashfield DCP 2016">
      <data key="d0">Inner West Ashfield DCP 2016</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Inner West Ashfield DCP 2016 is a document that outlines development control plans related to heritage and urban planning in the Inner West area.&lt;SEP&gt;The Inner West Ashfield DCP 2016 is a document that outlines heritage conservation principles and guidelines for properties within the Inner West area.&lt;SEP&gt;The Inner West Ashfield DCP 2016 is a planning document that outlines zoning and heritage conservation guidelines for the Inner West area.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e213365f9a7f0281bb90f965bf8564a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc1f8f1903ab76680b7ec87649559786&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00060f44e7476ee6d1aa588656bd98c6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
