    <node id="Council">
      <data key="d0">Council</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Council is the governing body responsible for assessing development applications and managing land contamination issues under various environmental acts.&lt;SEP&gt;The Council is responsible for overseeing site investigations and remediation plans as part of the development control process.&lt;SEP&gt;The Council is the governing body responsible for overseeing the development applications related to community gardens and other local regulations. It plays a crucial role in implementing the Development Control Plan, ensuring compliance with its regulations concerning land use and environmental management. Additionally, the Council is tasked with assessing development applications to ensure they meet relevant accessibility and safety standards. Through these responsibilities, the Council aims to facilitate sustainable development while adhering to community and environmental guidelines.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f28867a3fc10524b43c49ac8a114c352&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2baf67d66b01fda7f4e88a70305a53d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47f52554c6ddc5c2a86e6c2968f68139&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63b4b9dd8db1aaf82eb3cff13413e1e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-779ec25fbe5c026daa88c5a43c5f66e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b9b1e12f686047b31dc8c9ff5a2e0f4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1756462559</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Community Garden">
      <data key="d0">Community Garden</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Community Garden refers to a space where individuals can cultivate plants and vegetables, requiring a development application for establishment on private or council-owned land.&lt;SEP&gt;Community Gardens are designated areas where individuals can cultivate plants and vegetables, requiring a development application for establishment on private or council-controlled land.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a2baf67d66b01fda7f4e88a70305a53d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-779ec25fbe5c026daa88c5a43c5f66e5</data>
