    <node id="Clause C1">
      <data key="d0">Clause C1</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Clause C1 is a regulatory framework that encompasses several key aspects of urban planning and development. It addresses building height limits to ensure that new constructions are compatible with the surrounding street wall height, thereby maintaining the visual coherence of the area. Additionally, Clause C1 incorporates heritage considerations in residential development, ensuring that new projects do not adversely affect the cultural significance of the locality. It also pertains to land use zoning and outlines future development requirements as specified in the Leichhardt Development Control Plan (DCP) 2013. Furthermore, Clause C1 mandates that a comprehensive site and context analysis must be submitted for all new developments, with the exception of minor alterations, to ensure that all projects align with the established planning objectives.&lt;SEP&gt;Clause C1 pertains to development applications and compliance with relevant controls, including the Apartment Design Guide.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c559c94a28d4e3274c2163f18c72dae0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-489fcda892097faf351f3c6138355afb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e286e6413a0bfd476b033cc7b5ccfb77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bcafac0958c581e47c81e3b4834154f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56038c9ee33eb1b0d6b0916565a9fa1a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1756462150</data>
    </node>
