    <node id="Environmental Planning and Assessment Act 1979">
      <data key="d0">Environmental Planning and Assessment Act 1979</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Environmental Planning and Assessment Act 1979 is a key piece of legislation in New South Wales, Australia, that governs development applications, planning, and assessment processes. It establishes the framework for land use and development, ensuring that various factors, including environmental considerations and land contamination, are taken into account during development assessments. This Act plays a crucial role in regulating how land is utilized and developed within the region, promoting sustainable planning practices.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c90d09fd86358ff34cca423643290bd6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47f52554c6ddc5c2a86e6c2968f68139&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fc6ffe0c1dd4b4287d57f7cb7cdf731&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63b4b9dd8db1aaf82eb3cff13413e1e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a508bfc5d79a3f8e112147c41e0822e</data>
