    <edge source="IWLEP 2022" target="Leichhardt DCP 2013">
      <data key="d6">50.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Leichhardt DCP 2013 includes amendments from IWLEP 2022, indicating a relationship between the two planning documents.&lt;SEP&gt;The Leichhardt Development Control Plan (DCP) 2013 and the Inner West Local Environmental Plan (IWLEP) 2022 are both essential planning documents that govern land use in the Inner West region. The Leichhardt DCP 2013 incorporates amendments from the IWLEP 2022, highlighting a regulatory relationship between the two documents. Specifically, the Leichhardt DCP 2013 provides detailed development control guidelines that align with the broader framework established by the IWLEP 2022. This indicates that the development controls outlined in the Leichhardt DCP 2013 are amended and informed by the provisions of the IWLEP 2022, ensuring consistency and coherence in land use planning within the region.&lt;SEP&gt;Leichhardt DCP 2013 outlines development controls that may be influenced by the regulations set forth in IWLEP 2022.</data>
      <data key="d8">amendments,development control,development planning,land use,planning alignment,planning documents,planning regulations,regulatory framework</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-c559c94a28d4e3274c2163f18c72dae0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f832ae0e708eef5d6da39079c74ab40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed559eb921e82179a5ab2b83d8456566&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87f3217d092603d5e1a949d5ef9939fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a508bfc5d79a3f8e112147c41e0822e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-559fa0a250051042f9354b0984303a96</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1756462623</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="IWLEP 2022" target="Environmental Planning and Assessment Act 1979">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">IWLEP 2022 is developed under the framework of the Environmental Planning and Assessment Act 1979, establishing a legal basis for its provisions.</data>
      <data key="d8">planning legislation,regulatory framework</data>
