    <edge source="Heritage Conservation Areas" target="Leichhardt DCP 2013">
      <data key="d6">43.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Leichhardt DCP 2013 includes provisions for development within Heritage Conservation Areas, emphasizing the importance of heritage significance.&lt;SEP&gt;The Heritage Conservation Areas, as outlined in the Leichhardt DCP 2013, are subject to specific regulations designed to ensure that any developments within these areas are sensitive to their historical and cultural significance. The DCP mandates that developments must be responsive to the unique character of Heritage Conservation Areas, thereby promoting land uses that safeguard their values. Additionally, the document includes provisions aimed at protecting these areas, reinforcing its commitment to preserving their integrity and heritage. Overall, the Leichhardt DCP 2013 serves as a comprehensive framework for the conservation and protection of Heritage Conservation Areas, ensuring that their significance is maintained for future generations.</data>
      <data key="d8">development guidelines,heritage management,heritage preservation,heritage protection,regulatory framework,urban design,urban planning</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-2a31ca0ad7ef033136702ccbb86559a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72f295e95bd32e9a02119f496cba255c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22bb41e5d9af8e1f44c220ea3ef55754&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a508bfc5d79a3f8e112147c41e0822e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-559fa0a250051042f9354b0984303a96</data>
